{\pard\sb240\sa120\b\fs32\cf2 1. CrunchSumK0G0\par}
{\pard\sb120\b\fs24 Purpose: Sum ALL data (no grouping, no keys)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Function Signature:\par}
{\pard\li720\f1\fs18
private static void CrunchSumK0G0(CrunchLayout layout, ICrunchInputReader reader, ICrunchSumOutputWriter writer)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Parameters:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
\bullet  {\b layout}: Defines K=0, GroupCount=0, Mode=Sum\par
\bullet  {\b reader}: Reads rows from binary file or database\par
\bullet  {\b writer}: Writes output results\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Input Data Structure:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b k[]} (int array) - Key columns (empty for K=0)\par
{\b g[][]} (byte 2D array) - Group columns (empty for G=0)\par
{\b d[]} (sbyte array) - Dummy columns (usually 0 or 1 values)\par
{\b v[]} (double array) - Value columns (e.g., balance, contributions)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Output Structure:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b ki[]} (byte array) - Key indices (empty)\par
{\b kv[]} (int array) - Key values (empty)\par
{\b gi[]} (byte array) - Group indices (empty)\par
{\b gv[]} (byte array) - Group values (empty)\par
{\b DummySum[]} (int array) - Sum of dummy columns\par
{\b ValueSum[]} (double array) - Sum of value columns\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22\cf3 Example:\par}
{\pard\sb60\b Input Data (4 rows, 3 value columns):\par}
{\pard\li720\f1\fs18
Row 1: v = [1000.00, 500.00, 250.00]\par
Row 2: v = [2000.00, 800.00, 300.00]\par
Row 3: v = [1500.00, 600.00, 275.00]\par
Row 4: v = [1800.00, 700.00, 290.00]\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Processing:\par}
{\pard\li720\fs20
1. Create single CrunchSum accumulator\par
2. Read each row, add values to accumulator\par
3. Write single output row with totals\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Output (1 row):\par}
{\pard\li720\f1\fs18
ki=[], kv=[], gi=[], gv=[]\par
DummySum=[4]  (4 participants)\par
ValueSum=[6300.00, 2600.00, 1115.00]  (totals across all rows)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Array Index Meanings:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b v[0]} = First value column (e.g., total_balance)\par
{\b v[1]} = Second value column (e.g., contributions)\par
{\b v[2]} = Third value column (e.g., withdrawals)\par
{\b ValueSum[i]} = Sum of all rows for value column i\par}

\page

{\pard\sb240\sa120\b\fs32\cf2 2. CrunchSumK0G2\par}
{\pard\sb120\b\fs24 Purpose: Sum with 2-Dimensional Grouping (no keys)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Function Signature:\par}
{\pard\li720\f1\fs18
private static void CrunchSumK0G2(CrunchLayout layout, ICrunchInputReader reader, ICrunchSumOutputWriter writer)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Parameters:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
\bullet  {\b layout}: Defines K=0, GroupCount=2 (e.g., G1=3 mkt cols, G2=18 pop cols)\par
\bullet  {\b reader}: Reads participant data\par
\bullet  {\b writer}: Writes cross-tabulated results\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Input Data Structure:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b k[]} - Empty (K=0)\par
{\b g[0][]} - Dimension 0 values (e.g., 3 bytes for mkt_01, mkt_02, mkt_03)\par
{\b g[1][]} - Dimension 1 values (e.g., 18 bytes for pop_01, pop_02, ..., pop_74)\par
{\b d[]} - Dummy column (count=1 for active participant)\par
{\b v[]} - Value columns (e.g., balance, returns)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Output Structure:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b gi[0]} - Which column in dimension 0 (0=mkt_01, 1=mkt_02, 2=mkt_03)\par
{\b gi[1]} - Which column in dimension 1 (0=pop_01, 1=pop_02, ...)\par
{\b gv[0]} - Value from dimension 0 column (e.g., 2 = market segment 2)\par
{\b gv[1]} - Value from dimension 1 column (e.g., 3 = age bracket 3)\par
{\b DummySum[]} - Count of participants in this bucket\par
{\b ValueSum[]} - Sum of values for this bucket\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22\cf3 Example:\par}
{\pard\sb60\b Input Data (Participant-Level):\par}
{\pard\li720\f1\fs18
Row 1: g[0]=[2,1,3], g[1]=[1,0,2,...], v=[5000.00, 0.05], d=[1]\par
Row 2: g[0]=[2,1,3], g[1]=[1,0,2,...], v=[3000.00, 0.03], d=[1]\par
Row 3: g[0]=[3,2,1], g[1]=[2,1,1,...], v=[7000.00, 0.07], d=[1]\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Array Index Meanings:\par}
{\pard\li720\fs20
{\b g[0][0]} = Value in mkt_01 column (participant's market segment)\par
{\b g[0][1]} = Value in mkt_02 column (participant's sub-segment)\par
{\b g[0][2]} = Value in mkt_03 column (participant's plan size)\par
{\b g[1][0]} = Value in pop_01 column (participant's age bracket)\par
{\b g[1][1]} = Value in pop_02 column (participant's gender)\par
{\b g[1][2]} = Value in pop_03 column (participant's tenure)\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Memory Structure:\par}
{\pard\li720\f1\fs18
sum[ordinal][m][n] where:\par
  ordinal = column combination (0-53 for 3x18)\par
  m = group value from dimension 0 (0-max_mkt_value)\par
  n = group value from dimension 1 (0-max_pop_value)\par
\par
Example: sum[0][2][1] accumulates data for:\par
  - Column combo 0 (mkt_01 x pop_01)\par
  - mkt_01 value = 2\par
  - pop_01 value = 1\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Processing Algorithm:\par}
{\pard\li720\fs20
1. Allocate 4D array: sum[54][max_m+1][max_n+1]\par
2. For each participant row:\par
   - Extract g[0] and g[1] arrays\par
   - For each (i,j) combination:\par
     ordinal = i*18 + j\par
     sum[ordinal][g[0][i]][g[1][j]].Add(d, v)\par
3. Write output for all combinations where count > 0\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Output Example (Partial - 3 rows of ~1,000s):\par}
{\pard\li720\f1\fs18
gi=[0,0], gv=[2,1], DummySum=[2], ValueSum=[8000.00, 0.08]\par
  Meaning: mkt_01=2 AND pop_01=1, 2 participants, totals\par
\par
gi=[1,0], gv=[1,1], DummySum=[2], ValueSum=[8000.00, 0.08]\par
  Meaning: mkt_02=1 AND pop_01=1, 2 participants, totals\par
\par
gi=[0,0], gv=[3,2], DummySum=[1], ValueSum=[7000.00, 0.07]\par
  Meaning: mkt_01=3 AND pop_01=2, 1 participant, totals\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Total Output Rows:\par}
{\pard\li720\fs20
For G1=3, G2=18:\par
\bullet  54 column combinations (3 \'d7 18)\par
\bullet  Each combination has multiple (m, n) value pairs\par
\bullet  Typical output: 1,000 to 50,000 rows depending on data cardinality\par}

