{\pard\sb240\sa120\b\fs32\cf2 8. CrunchBoxK1G0\par}
{\pard\sb120\b\fs24 Purpose: Percentiles by Key (no grouping)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Function Signature:\par}
{\pard\li720\f1\fs18
private static void CrunchBoxK1G0(CrunchLayout layout, CrunchHeap heap, CrunchInputFileReader reader, ICrunchBoxOutputWriter writer)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Parameters:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
\bullet  {\b layout}: Defines K=1, GroupCount=0\par
\bullet  {\b heap}: Contains Key[0][r] values\par
\bullet  {\b reader}: Reads value columns\par
\bullet  {\b writer}: Writes percentiles for each key\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Input Data Structure:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b heap.Key[0][r]} - Key value for row r\par
{\b data[r]} - Value for row r in current column\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22 Output Structure:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b ki[0]} - Always 0\par
{\b kv[0]} - The key value\par
{\b gi[]} - Empty\par
{\b gv[]} - Empty\par
{\b vi} - Value column index\par
{\b vq} - Count of rows for this key\par
{\b vs[]} - 7 percentiles for this key\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs22\cf3 Example:\par}
{\pard\sb60\b Use Case: Plan-level participant distributions\par}
{\pard\li720\fs20
For each plan, compute percentiles of participant balances/returns\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Input Data in Heap:\par}
{\pard\li720\f1\fs18
Plan PLN001 (100 participants, rows 0-99):\par
  Key[0][0-99] = PLN001\par
  data[0-99] = participant balances\par
\par
Plan PLN002 (150 participants, rows 100-249):\par
  Key[0][100-249] = PLN002\par
  data[100-249] = participant balances\par
\par
Plan PLN003 (75 participants, rows 250-324):\par
  Key[0][250-324] = PLN003\par
  data[250-324] = participant balances\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Array Index Meanings:\par}
{\pard\li720\fs20
{\b keyq} = Number of unique keys\par
{\b rmin[b]} = Starting row for key block b\par
{\b rmax[b]} = Ending row + 1 for key block b\par
{\b va[]} = Array of values for current key\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Processing Algorithm:\par}
{\pard\li720\fs20
1. Scan heap to identify key boundaries:\par
   rmin[0]=0, rmax[0]=100 (PLN001)\par
   rmin[1]=100, rmax[1]=250 (PLN002)\par
   rmin[2]=250, rmax[2]=325 (PLN003)\par
\par
2. For each value column k:\par
   For each key block b:\par
     a. Count non-null values in data[rmin[b]:rmax[b]]\par
     b. Allocate va[vq]\par
     c. Copy non-null values into va\par
     d. Compute percentiles\par
     e. Write output row\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Output Example (1 value column, 3 plans):\par}
{\pard\li720\f1\fs18
ki=[0], kv=[PLN001], gi=[], gv=[], vi=0, vq=100\par
vs=[5000.00, 12000.00, 25000.00, 50000.00, 95000.00, 150000.00, 200000.00]\par
  Plan PLN001, balance column, 100 participants,\par
  P50 (median) = $50,000\par
\par
ki=[0], kv=[PLN002], gi=[], gv=[], vi=0, vq=150\par
vs=[3000.00, 8000.00, 20000.00, 45000.00, 85000.00, 140000.00, 190000.00]\par
  Plan PLN002, 150 participants, median = $45,000\par
\par
ki=[0], kv=[PLN003], gi=[], gv=[], vi=0, vq=75\par
vs=[8000.00, 15000.00, 30000.00, 60000.00, 110000.00, 175000.00, 225000.00]\par
  Plan PLN003, 75 participants, median = $60,000\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Interpretation:\par}
{\pard\li720\fs20
Each output row shows the distribution of participant values within that plan.\par
\par
Example for PLN001:\par
\bullet  P05 = $5,000: 5% of participants have balance \'a3 $5,000\par
\bullet  P25 = $25,000: 25% have balance \'a3 $25,000\par
\bullet  P50 = $50,000: Median (half above, half below)\par
\bullet  P75 = $95,000: 75% have balance \'a3 $95,000\par
\bullet  P95 = $200,000: 95% have balance \'a3 $200,000\par}

{\pard\sb60\b Output Volume:\par}
{\pard\li720\fs20
For 16 value columns, 1000 plans:\par
16 \'d7 1000 = 16,000 output rows (one per plan per column)\par}

