{\pard\sb240\sa120\b\fs32\cf5 Summary: Key Differences\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs24 Sum vs Box Mode:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b Sum Mode}:\par
\bullet  Reads data row-by-row\par
\bullet  Accumulates totals in memory\par
\bullet  Outputs: counts and sums\par
\bullet  Memory efficient for large datasets\par
\bullet  Output size proportional to unique combinations\par
\par
{\b Box Mode}:\par
\bullet  Loads ALL data into heap first\par
\bullet  Reads column-by-column\par
\bullet  Sorts values and computes percentiles\par
\bullet  Memory intensive (full dataset in RAM)\par
\bullet  Output size much larger (one row per bucket)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs24 K (Keys) Parameter:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b K=0}: Process all data together (global analysis)\par
{\b K=1}: Process separately for each key (per-plan, per-participant)\par
\par
Requirement: When K=1, input MUST be sorted by key column\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs24 G (Groups) Parameter:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b G=0}: No grouping (simple aggregation)\par
{\b G=1}: One dimension (e.g., 3 fund categories)\par
{\b G=2}: Two dimensions (e.g., 3 mkt \'d7 18 pop = 54 combos)\par
\par
Each participant row contributes to multiple output rows\par
(one for each group column combination)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs24 Output Array Conventions:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b ki[]} - Key indices (always [0] for K=1)\par
{\b kv[]} - Key values (actual IDs)\par
{\b gi[]} - Group indices (which columns)\par
{\b gv[]} - Group values (actual category codes)\par
{\b DummySum[]} - Row counts (Sum mode)\par
{\b ValueSum[]} - Column totals (Sum mode)\par
{\b vi} - Value column index (Box mode)\par
{\b vq} - Non-null value count (Box mode)\par
{\b vs[]} - 7 percentiles: P05, P10, P25, P50, P75, P90, P95 (Box mode)\par}

{\pard\sb120\b\fs24 Performance Characteristics:\par}
{\pard\li720\sb60
{\b Fastest}: K0G0 (single output row)\par
{\b Fast}: K1G0 (one row per key)\par
{\b Moderate}: K0G2, K1G1 (multiple groups)\par
{\b Memory-Intensive}: All Box modes (heap required)\par
{\b Largest Output}: BoxK0G2 with high cardinality groups\par}

